                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Posted in 28 Dec, 2017 - will update if there's a change (mainly on Cons section)\n\n[h1]Pros[/h1]\n+ Interesting setting, kinda like Hogwarts but in anime style\n+ The cast is alright ; MC isn't really your typical \"passive\" character and can be reliable when needed. The other characters is also okay with the exception of the 4 classmates (well, they're not really important so yea)\n+ \"Surprising\" BGM section, adding a personal commentary from the composer for every used track is a really nice value. Something that's not really (if ever) present in VN these days ~\n+ The art is nice especially those chibi one ! They need to add some of it to the store page\n+ As someone who doesn't read the full trilogy yet, I would say this is an alright introduction to the whole series. It completes their own individual mystery but left some of the bigger one for later, making you want to know more. \n\n[h1]Cons[/h1]\n- There are still some technical issue that needs to be solved. Some can be fixed by your own and some are not. For example, the blurry text and Steam not tracking the game properly. You can check the pinned post on the discussion forum to see how to fix these.\n- The game itself doesn't take too long to complete. Each route only takes around 2-3 hours to finish. This makes it hard to care more about each heroine especially Tsubaki and Neko.\n\n[h1]Conclusion[/h1]\nIf you like some light mystery sets in a magical school with a likable cast, feel free to give this one a try. It's in my opinion an okay introduction to the whole trilogy which i hope will be releasing soon ^^\n\n\n\nPS. Don't forget to apply some of the solution from the pinned post to solve your issues.",
